    "created_at": "2016-07-19T08:59:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-07-19T08:59:06Z",
    "body": "I think I would prefer that. We put `class` and `id` in DOM because they are \"superglobal attributes\". Features that are \"global attributes\" for a limited set of namespaces probably don't really belong in DOM directly, insofar we have any meaningful modularization here...\n\n@domenic agreed?\n",
